**Jiro** (Secondary). The local police captain, chronically overworked
and much too quick to draw his gun. As the local police captain, Jiro
keeps the force running, and the strain shows: he's jumpy, irritable,
and always juggling several unrelated jobs at once, sometimes
answering phones, barking orders, and doing paperwork all at the same
time. His colleagues keep urging him to take time off, but he's never
missed a day, and some suspect he's been saving up vacation for
decades. Whether from stress or something darker, he tends to aim his
gun at anything he considers an unwanted intrusion. *Armored +1
(Bulletproof Vest), Attack +1 (Police Training), Combat Expert +2,
Evasive +1, Intimidating +2, Minions +3 (Officers), Perceptive +1,
Position of Power +2, Strong +2, Tough +1; Compulsion −2
(Trigger-Happy), Dependency −1 (Coffee), Jittery −2, Obsession −3
(Work), Servitude −2 (Police Force), Short-Tempered −3, Stubborn −1.*
Desk-Side Revolver (Effective x2, Ranged; Ammunition, Weapon): Roll 4,
DX 4, End 0. Jiro's constant companion and likely only friend. Bare
Knuckle (Stunning; Inaccurate): Roll 3, DX 4, End 5. While he prefers
"civilized" weaponry like his revolver, Jiro can throw a mean punch.
Defense 3. Health 30, Endurance 20. TV 9.

